You can turn this on in TalkBack settings.␀**TalkBack can still describe text in images␀TalkBack gestures changed␀TalkBack has been updated␀ááTalkBack is a screen reader intended for situations or people who have difficulty seeing the screen. It gives you spoken feedback so that you can use your device without looking at the screen.

You can turn TalkBack on or off by holding both volume keys for several seconds.

When TalkBack is on, the focused item on the screen is spoken out loud.

Swiping right will move to the next item, and swiping left will move to the previous item.

Swipe right now to find the next button.␀TalkBack menu␀qqTalkBack now includes a braille keyboard so you can type faster with braille. To try it, go to TalkBack settings.␀TalkBack off␀TalkBack on␀TalkBack setting␀TalkBack settings␀uuTalkBack speech stopped. Usually, this will stop the current phrase that TalkBack is saying. Swipe right to continue.␀PPTalkBack turned on. To turn it off, touch and hold with 2 fingers for 5 seconds.␀TalkBack tutorial␀TalkBack will reset keymap␀::TalkBack will reset keymap and change modifier key to %1$s␀Tap␀  Tap %1$s to type the letter %2$s␀Tap and hold with 3 fingers␀::Tap dot 1 with your left index finger to type the letter A␀15Tap dot 1 with your left index finger to type â€œAâ€␀&&Tap once on a focused item to activate␀Tap to assign␀Tap to find out more␀::Tap to learn how to use TalkBack faster with new gestures.␀//Tap to review changes to accessibility gestures␀  Tap to switch to selecting a day␀!!Tap to switch to selecting a year␀Tap with 2 fingers␀Tap with 3 fingers␀Tap with 4 fingers␀Terms of service␀Text editing␀Text-to-speech settings␀$$The Notification Channel of TalkBack␀€€The TalkBack menu includes settings and controls that you may need often.

