Talkback has braille support, and uses Bluetooth to help you connect with a braille display.

To navigate using TalkBack:
â€¢ Swipe right or left to move between items
â€¢ Double-tap to activate an item
â€¢ Drag two fingers to scroll

To turn off TalkBack:
â€¢ Tap the switch. Youâ€™ll see a green outline. Double-tap the switch.
â€¢ On the confirmation message, tap OK. Then double-tap OK.␀FFWhen TalkBack is on, you can tap your screen to enter braille symbols.␀‚ì‚öWhen Talkback is on, it provides spoken feedback so that you can use your device without looking at the screen. Talkback is intended for situations or people who have difficulty seeing the screen.<br><br>Talkback has braille support, and uses Bluetooth to help you connect with a braille display.<br><br><b>How to use Talkback</b><br>â€¢ Swipe right or left to move between items<br>â€¢ Double-tap to activate an item<br>â€¢ Drag 2 fingers to scroll<br><br><b>How to turn off Talkback</b><br><br><b>Volume Keys:</b> Press &amp; hold both volume keys for a few seconds.<br><br><b>Settings</b><br>â€¢ Tap the <b>Use Talkback</b> switch. You&apos;ll see a green outline. Double-tap the switch.<br>â€¢ On the confirmation message, tap stop. Then double-tap Stop.␀When lock screen is shown␀€Ù€ÙWhen you activate a text box, a keyboard opens at the bottom of your screen.

