Youâ€™re using Unified English Braille. To switch your input language, go to TalkBack settings.␀DHYour %1$s should be on dot 1. Now, tap dot 1 to type the letter â€œAâ€.␀LLGet spoken feedback so you can use your watch without looking at the screen.␀€Œ€ŒTalkBack is a screen reader primarily for people with blindness and low vision. It allows interaction with the device using spoken feedback.␀google-sans␀google-sans-medium␀ÅË<b>How to use TalkBack</b><br>â€¢ Swipe right or left to move between items<br>â€¢ Double-tap to activate an item<br>â€¢ Drag 2 fingers to scroll<br><br><b>How to turn off TalkBack</b><br><br><b>Volume keys:</b> Press and hold both volume keys for a few seconds<br><br><b>Settings</b><br>1. Tap <b>Use TalkBack</b>. There will be a green outline. Double-tap it.<br>2. On the confirmation message, tap <b>Stop</b>. There will be a green outline. Double-tap it.␀€ª€ªTalkBack provides spoken feedback so that you can use your device without looking at the screen. TalkBack can be helpful for people who have difficulty seeing the screen.␀"%1$s" o "%2$s" para i-adjust␀"%1$s" para isaayos␀
